{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Gather and hear.</b> He mentioned to them his two names, Jacob and Israel, and he mentioned the sons alongside Jacob, because at the time his name was Jacob he had the sons, and afterward he was called by the name Israel, as it was said to him (Genesis 32:29): ״לא יעקב יאמר עוד שמך כי אם ישראל״. It is also possible to interpret ״הקבצו ושמעו״ — 'gather and hear' — as referring to the words of the sons of Jacob: and what are all the words that you shall hear? — to the Holy One, blessed be He; this is ״ושמעו אל ישראל אביכם״ — 'and hear, O Israel, your father' — who is in heaven, Israel the Elder; and therefore he doubled the hearing." "<b>And I found</b> support for this in what they said in the Midrash: A parable — to what may the matter be compared? To a servant whom the king trusted with all that he has. That servant came to die; he called his sons to declare them free men and to say to them: Where are your deeds of title? The king came and saw that servant expounding the matter at length to them. He said to them: I beg you, the king's servants — honor him just as I honored him all my days. So too our father Jacob called his sons to inform them of the end. Immediately the Holy One, blessed be He, was revealed upon him. He said to him: To your sons you call, but to Me you do not call? As it is said (Isaiah 43:22): ״ולא אותי קראת יעקב״. When Jacob saw Him, he began and said to his sons: I ask of you, honor the Holy One, blessed be He, in the manner that my fathers honored Him, as it is said (Genesis 48:15): ״האלהים אשר התהלכו אבותי לפניו״, etc. They said to him: We know what is in your heart: ״שמע ישראל ה׳ אלהינו ה׳ אחד״. When Jacob heard this, he bowed upon the bed, as it is said: ״וישתחו ישראל על ראש המטה״. And he said in a whisper: Blessed be the name of His glorious kingdom forever and ever."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:20.761736131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}